# Environment Variables — SplitPay

# No environment variables are required to run SplitPay locally or to deploy it.
# All bill calculations and QR code generation run entirely in the browser.
# No Firebase SDK, API key, database, or backend is needed for this version.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Firebase Hosting (optional — for deploy only)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Instead of using environment variables, Firebase Hosting uses `.firebaserc`
# to remember your project alias locally. Copy `.firebaserc.example` to
# `.firebaserc` and fill in your Firebase project ID.
#
# Example:
#   cp .firebaserc.example .firebaserc
#   # then edit .firebaserc and set your project ID
#
# Deploy without a local alias:
#   npm run deploy -- --project YOUR_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID
#
# See docs/FIREBASE_HOSTING.md for a full deployment walkthrough.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Future integrations
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# If you add a backend (e.g. webhook verification, authenticated merchants),
# add the required variables here with placeholder values and document them.
#
# Example:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com
# VITE_MERCHANT_SECRET=your-secret-here
